      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dubuque is Iowa’s oldest city and one of the oldest settlements west of the Mississippi River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofdubuque.org/1060/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from Julien Dubuque, a French-Canadian prospector who settled near the Mississippi and ran the Mines of Spain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubuque%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dubuque’s Shot Tower, one of the few remaining lead‑shot factories, is a National Historic Landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubuque%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Julien Dubuque Bridge, built in 1943, carries traffic across the Mississippi and is also a National Historic Landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubuque%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Fenelon Place Elevator, the world’s oldest electric funicular, climbs 150 feet up the bluffs in downtown Dubuque.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubuque%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The National Mississippi River Museum & Aquarium showcases river culture and displays Gulf of Mexico wildlife right on the riverfront.",
